    "shop_smart":  [
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eRice and green beans are the volume, and both are cheap.\u003c/strong\u003e That is why this stays easy on the budget despite having real beef in it.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eFrozen green beans beat fresh here.\u003c/strong\u003e They get simmered into the beef anyway, so the snap does not matter, and the bag price per pound is far lower.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eTurmeric and cinnamon are pennies per batch.\u003c/strong\u003e Persian cooking gets its depth from spices you already own rather than from expensive ingredients.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eDo not skip the tahdig step even though it is optional.\u003c/strong\u003e The oil in the bottom of the pot costs nothing and it turns a good rice dish into the one people ask you to make again."
